WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.065 --> 00:00:01.670
(grunting)

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:02.878
- Fucking shit!

00:00:02.878 --> 00:00:04.022
(laughing)

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:07.697
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:07.697 --> 00:00:09.447
- Tap, tap, tap, tap.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.763
- Hey guys we're at Ncuti's House.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.760
(Ncuti laughing)

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.580
And we're gonna be
- Welcome to the crib.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.778
- I love your house, Ncuti.
- Thank you.

00:00:18.778 --> 00:00:19.760
- It's so nice, look at all the art.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.673
- This is what happens
when you're in Vogue,

00:00:21.673 --> 00:00:23.025
you get a house like this.
- [Kedar] Yeah.

00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:24.560
(Ncuti laughs)

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.980
- We are gonna find out
who is the best gamer,

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.335
so lets play and let's find out.

00:00:29.335 --> 00:00:31.760
(techno music)

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.569
- Obviously I'm Donkey Kong.

00:00:33.569 --> 00:00:35.560
- [Connor] Do you remember
the controls, Ncuti?

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.393
- No!

00:00:36.393 --> 00:00:38.470
Nobody's explained it.
- All right, so this is go,

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:39.333
this is break,

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.323
this is drift.

00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:42.156
(Kedar imitating car drifting)

00:00:42.156 --> 00:00:43.850
All right, what's the fun
stage, we want a fun one.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.683
Here we go.

00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:46.990
- Oh my god so this is what I was playing

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.060
in season one.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.322
Wait I really, that was some real acting.

00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:52.765
(game countdown beeping)

00:00:52.765 --> 00:00:53.598
- Bro...
(laughing)

00:00:53.598 --> 00:00:54.974
- You pressed pause, bruh.

00:00:54.974 --> 00:00:56.676
- What happened?
(laughing)

00:00:56.676 --> 00:01:00.020
- [Connor] Ncuti is top
right, I am bottom right,

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.200
Asa is top left,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.271
Kedar is bottom left.
- [Kedar] Is the winner.

00:01:04.271 --> 00:01:07.051
- [Asa] Come and get me. Watch
out for my banana though.

00:01:07.051 --> 00:01:08.080
- All right you dropped it there,

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.877
but lucky for you, there was
a big ass cow in the way.

00:01:10.877 --> 00:01:12.080
- Mooove, blud.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.160
You get it?

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:13.993
That was clever.

00:01:13.993 --> 00:01:15.578
- [Connor] Are you breaking
as you go around corners, Asa?

00:01:15.578 --> 00:01:16.790
- [Asa] Yeah.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:17.623
- You break?

00:01:17.623 --> 00:01:18.739
- Tightly, I just tap the break once.

00:01:18.739 --> 00:01:20.980
- You tap it once, you tap the break once?

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.830
- Yeah, I will tap that break.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:23.663
- Tap that break.

00:01:23.663 --> 00:01:24.880
- Right.
- What's break again?

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.555
- [Asa] Ncuti you're going backwards!

00:01:26.555 --> 00:01:29.845
- Oh my fucking word, this is a piss take!

00:01:29.845 --> 00:01:32.000
(Kedar laughs)

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.195
I've ended up somehow on the ceiling.

00:01:34.195 --> 00:01:37.048
(Kedar laughs)
- Get your hand out my face.

00:01:37.048 --> 00:01:38.760
Do you know what I've just realized?

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.660
I'm gonna have to sacrifice
comedic commentary

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.580
to win.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.197
Why am I not turning?

00:01:44.197 --> 00:01:45.970
- [Asa] No, watch out!

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.017
- Yeah!
- No!

00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:49.306
(yelling)

00:01:49.306 --> 00:01:51.389
descending game bleeping)

00:01:52.514 --> 00:01:53.347
- Has everyone finished?

00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:55.502
(slight laughter)

00:01:55.502 --> 00:01:56.335
This is...

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:58.926
- You lot, go start dinner, yeah?

00:01:58.926 --> 00:02:00.762
(Kedar laughs) I'll be with you in a sec.

00:02:00.762 --> 00:02:01.914
(slight laughter)

00:02:01.914 --> 00:02:03.514
(soft music)

00:02:03.514 --> 00:02:05.910
- Oi oi, so what've we got 'ere then?

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:06.933
I have brought,

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.220
Some jollof, Ghanaian jollof.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.150
and I've brought kelewele.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.513
Now obviously,

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.060
Eric is half Nigerian, half Ghanaian

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.200
so that's why I brought some jollof.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.950
- Fresh out the oven?
- And some plantains

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.880
fresh out the oven!

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.995
We only do fresh cooking around here.

00:02:23.995 --> 00:02:25.040
No takeaway shit.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.573
- Ncuti didn't tell us
that he was cooking.

00:02:26.573 --> 00:02:27.930
- I brought some sushi.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.518
Here we go, I've got some soy sauce.

00:02:29.518 --> 00:02:31.930
- But the thing is, I didn't
actually cook it though,

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.080
you know that isn't it?

00:02:34.798 --> 00:02:36.155
(laughs loudly)

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.050
- Anyway, I've brought like a china mas--

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:38.883
Like, not even china masala,

00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:40.600
like a sort of Indian kind of ting,

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.540
just safety, innit?

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.010
- Some garlic naan.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:43.907
Love a nice garlic naan.

00:02:43.907 --> 00:02:45.026
- [Asa] Garlic naan?
- Garlic naan.

00:02:45.026 --> 00:02:46.510
You not a fan of garlic naan?

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.140
- I usually go for plain
though, to be honest.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:48.973
- Just plain?
- Really?

00:02:48.973 --> 00:02:49.806
- Just bread?

00:02:49.806 --> 00:02:50.639
- [Asa] Yeah.

00:02:50.639 --> 00:02:52.660
- And I bought a pizza, it didn't come.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.580
- It didn't come (laughs).

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.413
- There you go.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.232
- [All Together] Cheers!

00:02:59.232 --> 00:03:00.640
- Should we start sharing
out some of your food?

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.434
- Yeah, lets eat.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:03.490
- Oh, yes!

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.950
- Smash, cup, bam!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.180
Pizza's here.
- Pizza's here, bam!

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.270
Thanks.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.323
Thank you, sir.

00:03:09.456 --> 00:03:12.030
- [Connor] What is that?
- [Ncuti] It's plantain.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.160
- What color did you say this was?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.440
- Have I got any?

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.460
There seems to be a film
crew (laughs loudly)

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.293
My god!

00:03:18.293 --> 00:03:19.392
What are you guys doing here?

00:03:19.392 --> 00:03:20.452
- Got a question,

00:03:20.452 --> 00:03:22.273
from the question box.

00:03:22.273 --> 00:03:23.310
(plastic bag rustling)

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.870
I'd love you to keep
going through that bag

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:25.703
as I'm about to read.

00:03:25.703 --> 00:03:26.555
- (laughing) Go on.

00:03:28.511 --> 00:03:29.970
(giggling)

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.115
- Who surprised you the most

00:03:31.115 --> 00:03:33.340
once you got to know them on set?

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.320
- Probably you, Connor.
- Connor.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.504
- Yeah.
- Yeah, Connor.

00:03:35.504 --> 00:03:39.020
- That's our laugh because it's you!

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.151
- Yeah, it's me.

00:03:40.151 --> 00:03:41.292
(laughs loudly)

00:03:41.292 --> 00:03:43.330
- He's just very sweet.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:46.248
He is a very, very sweet, lovely boy.

00:03:46.248 --> 00:03:49.550
Okay, so what's the weirdest
thing you've been asked

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:51.515
in an interview, in an audition.

00:03:51.515 --> 00:03:53.890
We don't interview (laughs).

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.140
- I've done an air kiss in an audition

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.440
where in the sides it
said, "And now they kiss"

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.263
and I've gone (blows kiss)

00:04:01.263 --> 00:04:03.751
- Have you? (laughs)

00:04:03.751 --> 00:04:04.750
- What happened?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.280
- I think they were
like, "could you try it,

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.254
could you try to make it
a little more, kind of..."

00:04:11.254 --> 00:04:12.087
- Urban.

00:04:12.087 --> 00:04:14.142
- You know that one? (laughs loudly)

00:04:14.142 --> 00:04:15.656
You know that one there!

00:04:15.656 --> 00:04:17.430
Make it a little bit more urban.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.990
- What's the most show-biz
thing you've ever done,

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.390
or experienced?

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.390
- Present in a BAFTA.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.113
It was pretty, it felt pretty show-biz.

00:04:27.113 --> 00:04:29.590
Because that was weird,
just it looked like

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:31.640
Madame Tussauds, but everyone was moving.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:34.535
I was like, rah, this is real.

00:04:34.535 --> 00:04:36.780
Like, everyone was moving.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.200
That was pretty exciting.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.985
- If you could cast yourself in any part

00:04:40.985 --> 00:04:43.472
from any film ever, what would you be?

00:04:43.472 --> 00:04:45.389
- Neo in "The Matrix".

00:04:45.389 --> 00:04:46.660
- That's a good one.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.890
- Yeah.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:48.730
- Jay Gatsby.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:50.374
- I almost called my cat Gatsby.

00:04:50.374 --> 00:04:52.170
- It's a good cat name.
- Yeah!

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.590
they've got mustache, no?

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.318
- Well, they've got whiskers.

00:04:55.318 --> 00:04:57.260
- Would you rather win an Oscar,

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.384
or get to travel to space?

00:04:59.384 --> 00:05:01.172
- Travel to space.
- What?

00:05:01.172 --> 00:05:03.780
- An Oscar would look better on my social.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.757
- Oh my days.

00:05:04.757 --> 00:05:09.510
- (laughing loudly) No, travel
to space, travel to space.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.620
- Connor is not a fan.
- (laughing) He's not a fan.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.573
- Head in hands.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.590
- I wouldn't even do
it if it was 100% safe.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:17.423
- Really?

00:05:17.423 --> 00:05:20.400
(Ncuti laughs loudly)

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.570
- What do you miss most

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.280
when you're not on the set of Sex Ed?

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.400
- The people.
- Yeah.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.640
- I see you guys now and then,

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.749
but a lot of most of the
crew I don't see until

00:05:29.749 --> 00:05:32.360
at like a screening, or
people are in London,

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.533
or we go back to Wales.

00:05:34.994 --> 00:05:37.514
- I'll be brutally honest,
I didn't hear the question.

00:05:37.514 --> 00:05:38.613
(slight laughter)

00:05:38.613 --> 00:05:41.470
- Did you do any particular
research for your role;

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.380
how did you get into character?

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:46.080
- I chatted to my mom a bit
because my mom's a therapist,

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.561
but I didn't really do
anything to get into character.

00:05:48.561 --> 00:05:50.780
- I guess I looked to the
relationship I have with my mom,

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.250
and how strong that is

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.770
and how much of an
influence that has had on me

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:55.800
I guess, as I've grown up.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:59.320
- What's the best and worst
parts about your jobs as actors?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.317
- Best part of acting I
think is meeting people

00:06:01.317 --> 00:06:03.160
who you'd never get to meet

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.970
and kind of form friendships
and relationships.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.340
Worst part of acting.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.060
- I think what you said
before about the fact

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.040
you know, you get to
meet people and stuff.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.640
I think for me, that what happens after

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.420
you have to then just
say bye to those people

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:15.470
that you form this thing with,

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.030
that you'll never actually get again.

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:19.097
- So you're saying that the
best and worst part about it

00:06:19.097 --> 00:06:19.930
is the same thing?

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:21.220
- I find it.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:22.760
- You've got the wettest meals,

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.710
have you just got soups?

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.450
- Thanks for watching.
- Thanks for watching.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:27.623
- Thanks for watching.

